<title>UK: Yemen, Malta join International Grains Council.</title>
<headline>Yemen, Malta join International Grains Council.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Yemen has become a member of the London-based International Grains Council (IGC) effective from January 1997, the IGC said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>IGC members meeting in London on Tuesday approved Yemen's application as an importing member.</p>
<p>The Council also approved a membership application by Malta.</p>
<p>The IGC, representing importing and exporting countries, monitors world grains supply and demand.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 8072</p>
